[sliver] These are the 0.6 mm retaining lips on the two tabs. The receiving slots leave 0.45 mm nominal engagement. Their square catches retain the plate, and the noses taper toward the free ends. The face-down native slice retains approximately 0.607 mm of lip projection and generates no support on the plate; catch finish and force remain physical-print readings.
